.TH REMOTERIG-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "RemoteRig 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remoterig\-server \- share an amateur radio transceiver over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remoterig\-server
.RI [ --headless " [" --config " " FILE "] [" \-v ]]
.RI [ --list-audio ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs next to the transceiver and serves its audio, PTT and CAT control to a
remote client. Radio control goes through Hamlib, or through plain RTS/DTR
toggling on a serial port for rigs without CAT.
.PP
Audio travels over UDP, control over TCP. The PTT is sent on both at once, so a
lost datagram never leaves the rig transmitting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without a desktop session, logging to standard output. The settings are the
ones saved by the graphical interface: configure once with a display, then run
without one.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read an .ini file instead of the saved settings. Lets one machine serve several
rigs, each with its own file and ports.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also log frequency and mode changes. Without it, only transmit switches,
connections and errors are logged.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-audio
Print every audio interface and device PortAudio can see, with the sample rate
each one accepts, then exit. Use this when a device is missing from the lists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RR_HAMLIB_DEBUG
Set to 1 to let Hamlib print its own debug trace. It is silenced by default:
Hamlib repeats messages such as
.RB \(aq "no get_vfo" \(aq
on every poll, which buries the server's own log. Raise it only to diagnose a
CAT problem.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/F4JTV/RemoteRigServer.conf
Settings: radio model, serial port, audio devices, network ports.
.SH NOTES
Opening a serial port requires membership of the
.B dialout
group.
.PP
A systemd user unit is installed. Enable it with
.RB "\(aq" "systemctl --user enable --now remoterig-server" "\(aq" ,
and allow it to run without an open session with
.RB "\(aq" "sudo loginctl enable-linger $USER" "\(aq" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR remoterig-client (1),
.BR rigctl (1)
